 # M3 GPU backend — full-suite gate census (round 15)
 
+## Final technical-release contract — 2026-08-18
+
+The strict release census remains exactly **1,003** static shader identities through an
+explicit, semantically checked substitution. The Metal-only `fullscreen_blit` identity is
+absent; the genuine `draw_debug_draw_compact` WebGPU compute prepass is present and preserves
+debug-line lifetime compaction without illegal vertex-stage storage writes. The release
+runner requires all 1,003 named results to PASS, a cold cache of 1,003 unique MISS rows/files,
+a warm cache of 1,003 unique HIT rows, and zero uncaptured WebGPU device errors across each
+complete raw invocation (including asynchronous errors before BEGIN or after END). Result/cache
+logs must also contain zero `Error: Not freed memory blocks` reports. Result/cache rows remain
+confined to the exact census boundaries. A same-count transcript that retains
+`fullscreen_blit` or omits the
+compute prepass is an explicit negative fixture.
+
+The cache-result reporter is source-bound and fail-closed against early fixture work: when
+`BW_SHADER_CACHE_CENSUS_DIR` is present, it emits nothing until the active
+`BW_SHADER_CACHE_DIR` is nonempty and byte-equal to the census directory. This keeps GPU
+initialization builtins from reserving first-result identities and hiding the later static-loop
+HIT rows; adversarial checks reject a removed suppression or directory-equality guard.
+
+The canonical M3 build requires `WITH_OPENSUBDIV=ON` (so the four subdiv shaders use the
+harvested GLSL patch-basis source) and `WITH_GPU_DRAW_TESTS=ON`. Draw runtime coverage is a
+separate exact two-row `DrawWebGPUTest` supplement—`draw_curves_lib` and
+`draw_debug_lifetime_rebind`—rather than broadening every generic draw test to WebGPU. Its
+raw list and both RUN/OK logs are digest-bound and independently reparsed with zero device errors.
+The primary 197-test list is likewise bound as raw sole-suite stdout plus empty stderr and matched
+against a checked-in fully-qualified sorted identity manifest. Individual RUN/OK records are
+full-line anchored; suffix aliases are fatal.
+
+OpenSubdiv acceptance is separately receipt-bound to v3_7_0 / MD5
+`470d53c4d4335a601c33a052ce7c33b4`, its recipe/configuration and upstream selection sources,
+the harvested GLSL header plus CPU/GPU archives, archive member/symbol/no-OpenGL proofs, and a
+Wasm smoke returning Far level-1 vertex count 26 with both patch-basis source markers present.
+The verifier independently re-runs the bound archive member/symbol commands and smoke and compares
+their exact output. Pre/post snapshots cover all OpenSubdiv proof inputs, the native binary/build
+graph, and both canonical identity manifests; a final Ninja no-work proof closes the execution
+window. Cold and warm static identities must equal the checked-in sorted 1,003-name manifest.
+
+The M3 receipt additionally binds three device-creation sources by path, byte count, and SHA-256:
+native GHOST, browser GHOST fallback, and worker preinitialization. The runner and verifier
+independently require the exact same ten adapter-supported limit assignments in all three,
+exactly once per field, including `maxSampledTexturesPerShaderStage` and
+`maxSamplersPerShaderStage`; missing, duplicate, wrong-source, and cross-field values are fatal.
+
+## Current closeout reconciliation — 2026-08-11
+
+The authoritative current binary is `build-native-gpu/bin/tests/blender_test`; the
+`2026-08-11T14:42:24Z` `harness/run.sh --scope m3` receipt is **5/5 GREEN**. The suite now
+enumerates **196 tests: 189 PASS / 6 FAIL / 1 CRASH**. The remaining non-passes are:
+
+- `static_shaders` — aggregate failure described below;
+- `buffer_texture` — documented R32F blacklist tail;
+- `shader_sampler_argument_buffer_binding` — documented Metal-only blacklist artifact;
+- `framebuffer_subpass_input` — registered `subpass-input-attachment` deferral;
+- `texture_roundtrip__GPU_DATA_FLOAT__GPU_DEPTH_COMPONENT32F` and
+  `texture_roundtrip__GPU_DATA_FLOAT__GPU_DEPTH32F_STENCIL8` — registered
+  `depth-aspect-buffer-upload` deferral;
+- `shader_texture_atomic` — signal-11 crash after the registered storage-texture-atomic compile
+  rejection.
+
+The static shader library grew from 973 to **1003** entries and is **995/1003**. All eight
+non-compiles remain mapped: one `gpu_texture_atomic_test` (`OpImageTexelPointer`), two
+vertex-stage read-write storage shaders (`draw_curves_test`, `draw_debug_draw_display`), four
+runtime-generated OpenSubdiv placeholders, and the Metal-only `fullscreen_blit` artifact.
+
+Three former expected non-passes now pass and were removed from the fail-closed expectation map:
+`framebuffer_subpass_input_clearops`, `specialization_constants_graphic`, and
+`vertex_buffer_fetch_mode__GPU_COMP_I10__GPU_FETCH_INT_TO_FLOAT_UNIT`. The corresponding floors
+were raised, not weakened: GPU PASS minimum 148 to 189 and static compile minimum 956 to 995.
+
+Patches `0117-gpu-webgpu-diag-readback.patch` and
+`0125-gpu-webgpu-render-result-bridge.patch` are retained only as diagnostic history. Their
+private `BW_DIAG` bridge was superseded by the public production readback implementation
+(`GPU_readback.hh` and `wgpu_readback.*`), and the active source no longer contains the diagnostic
+files or hooks. Both M1 and M3 patch-consistency gates contain a literal two-name retirement
+allowlist that fails closed if either file or any `wgpu_diag_readback`, `webgpu::diag::`, or
+`diag::on_texture_read` payload reappears; arbitrary patch conflicts are still rejected.
+
+The remainder of this note is the historical round-15 characterization that established the
+original deferral and blacklist classes.
+
